	"versionControl": {
		"head": "k45g",
		"edges": [
			{
				"from": "k45a",
				"to": "k45a2",
				"comment": "Skylights: north and south facing chosen separately, each yes/no with its own area; skylight area moved off the roof"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45a2",
				"to": "k45b",
				"comment": "Roof only: skylights back on the roof, one shared skylight area, NE and SW skylight each yes/no"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45b",
				"to": "k45c",
				"comment": "Roof only: either no skylights, or a skylight area with at least one of NE/SW; if NE is added, SW is optional, and the other way round"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45c",
				"to": "k45c2",
				"comment": "Roof only, alternative to k45c (not in the parse list): NE and SW skylight chosen separately, each either left out or given its own area"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45c",
				"to": "k45d",
				"comment": "New set-up: roof windows, terrain and tinyhouses; original roof area (1062.7) and original terrain area (1866.2) kept constant; SW/NE roof window area, terrain open area, number, levels and size of tinyhouses"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45d",
				"to": "k45e",
				"comment": "Construction added: original construction constant, ventilation open/closed, insulation U1/U2; original roof and terrain areas dropped. Notes: open ventilated: no need to insulate k45; closed ventilation: can be either insulated or not; closed + insulated = hothouse; uninsulated: can be either open/close - can then insulate tinyhouse; removing concrete reduces embedded CO2, but gains green - what is tradeoff?; leveling out terrain - more original terrain remove, less concrete need to level it; surface is uneven, so if you leave it then need concrete to level it; this should appear from the numbers; energy performance"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45e",
				"to": "k45f",
				"comment": "Ventilation and insulation chosen as pairs: open + U1 or closed + U2. Notes from last meeting (10-01-2024): open ventilated: no need to insulate k45; closed ventilation: can be either insulated or not; closed + insulated = hothouse; uninsulated: can be either open/close - can then insulate tinyhouse; of interest: removing concrete reduces embedded CO2, but gains green - what is tradeoff?; leveling out terrain - more original terrain remove, less concrete need to level it; surface is uneven, so if you leave it then need concrete to level it; this should appear from the numbers; energy performance KPI is being developed by [...]"
			},
			{
				"from": "k45f",
				"to": "k45g",
				"comment": "Design concepts A, B and C via gaps l_gap1/l_gap2; interior deck width and facade length replace roof windows, terrain and tinyhouses. Design concepts: A: l_gap1 and l_gap2 both 0, one building; B: l_gap1 = 0 and l_gap2 = 5, one housing area detached from one common area (two buildings); C: l_gap1 and l_gap2 both 5, two housing areas detached from one common area (three buildings); no_deck_width (b1) decides the distance from facade (in either side) to the interior first floor deck; housing_length (Lf1 and Lf2) decides the length of the facade of the housing area. For later, of interest: removing concrete reduces embedded CO2, but gains green - what is tradeoff?; leveling out terrain - more original terrain remove, less concrete need to level it; surface is uneven, so if you leave it then need concrete to level it; this should appear from the numbers; energy performance KPI is being developed by [...]"
			}
		]
	},

